---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Home">
    <article class="home-bio">
        <h1>Saksham Gupta</h1>

        <div class="bio-content">
            <p>
                I build systems, abstractions, and platforms that make other engineers more
                productive.
            </p>

            <p>
                At my core, I am drawn to the mechanics of software: how it compiles, runs, and
                distributes. My interests sit at the intersection of backend systems and platform
                architecture, where I enjoy turning complex problems into clean, extensible
                abstractions.
            </p>

            <p>
                I like understanding systems by recreating them. When I want to learn how something
                works, I explore it through hands-on projects, whether that means writing a 32-bit
                UNIX clone kernel from scratch, building custom parsers, or digging into runtime
                internals. Currently, I am digging deep into distributed systems and reading <em
                    >Designing Data-Intensive Applications</em
                >.
            </p>

            <p>This blog is where I document and write about these deep dives.</p>

            <p class="blog-cta">
                <a href="/blog">Read the blog →</a>
            </p>
        </div>
    </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
    .home-bio {
        max-width: 70ch;
        margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .home-bio h1 {
        font-size: 2.5rem;
        margin-top: 0;
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .bio-content {
        margin-top: 2.5rem;
        font-size: 1.15rem;
        line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .bio-content p {
        margin-bottom: 1.8rem;
    }

    .blog-cta {
        margin-top: 3rem;
    }

    .blog-cta a {
        font-weight: 600;
        text-decoration: none;
    }

    .blog-cta a:hover {
        text-decoration: underline;
    }
</style>
